## Quick Comparison

| Language | Key Mechanism | Polling / Event |
|----------|--------------|-----------------|
| **TypeScript** | Node.js `fs.createReadStream` + interval polling (200 ms) | Continuous read loop via `setInterval` |
| **Python** | File re-read in a loop every 0.1 s, tracking last line | Polling with `time.sleep(0.1)` |
| **Go** | Buffered reader (`bufio.Scanner`) + goroutine poller | Goroutine keeps scanning until no more data |
| **Bash** | Shell builtin `tail -f` in background process | Uses system's native tail behavior |

All four functions share the same core idea: keep track of the most recent line printed and emit any new lines that differ from it as they appear on disk.
